@startuml
title SplitSmart use cases — complete product (proposed; desktop subset only)
left to right direction
actor User
actor Organizer
actor Approver
rectangle "SplitSmart complete product\n(web, Android, iOS; shared services proposed)" {
 usecase "Create account / sign in" as UC1
 usecase "Manage groups and members" as UC2
 usecase "Submit expense and receipt" as UC3
 usecase "Review / approve / reject" as UC4
 usecase "View expenses and balances" as UC5
 usecase "Record payment" as UC6
 usecase "Receive expense notice" as UC7
 usecase "Generate report" as UC8
}
User --> UC1
User --> UC3
User --> UC5
User --> UC6
User --> UC7
User --> UC8
Organizer --> UC2
Organizer --> UC4
Approver --> UC4
note bottom of UC3: Payer is separate from participants; may be excluded.
note bottom of UC4: Pending/rejected expenses do not affect balances.
note bottom of UC5: Swing MVP is desktop-only and does not satisfy platform scope.
@enduml
